+## Rotating the password
+
+To rotate the `password` without signing everyone out, set the new one as `password` and keep the previous one in `extraUnsealPasswords`.
+
+```js
+import { useSession } from "h3";
+
+app.use(async (event) => {
+  const session = await useSession(event, {
+    password: process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD, // new
+    extraUnsealPasswords: [process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD_OLD], // previous
+  });
+  return { id: session.id };
+});
+```
+
+Sessions are always sealed with `password`. Extra passwords are only used to unseal, tried in order after `password`, and a session cookie opened with one of them is resealed with `password` on that request. A session read from the session header cannot be resealed, so it keeps the old seal until it expires.
+
+> [!NOTE]
+> Every extra password costs one more key derivation when a session fails to open, so keep the list short. Remove an old password once `maxAge` has passed since the rotation. Until then, anyone holding it can still open sessions.
+
 ## Get Data from a Session
 
 To get data from a session, we will still use `useSession`. Under the hood, it will use `getSession` to get the session.
